node_definition.done_when:
Deliver §7 of docs/plans/lane-and-model-routing.html exactly as that section states. The plan and its locked decisions are the authority. §1 and §2 are on main: the catalogue docs/state/reckon/model-catalogue.yaml declares lanes and a top-level aliases table, mapping claude-opus, claude-haiku, codex-astra, codex-luna, codex-terra, codex-spark and clive-glm to lane and model key.

1. Add one read-side resolver, resolve_name(name) returning (lane, model_key). It reads the catalogue's alias table and the declared lanes. It accepts backend names, model ids and aliases, because stored reviews already mix those vocabularies. Use it in the ledger (reckon/ledger.py), run records and reviews (reckon/crew/recovery.py), review_excluded_backends, and the crew views (reckon/mcp_views.py, reckon/crew/reports.py). Rewrite no committed row. review_excluded_backends keeps working verbatim.
2. tests/test_old_names_resolve.py:
   - fixture rows written as claude-opus, and as claude with model opus, normalise identically;
   - all seven legacy names are exercised;
   - reckon crew ledger and runs report the lane-and-model pair for old rows;
   - the existing check that no routing identifier leaks into reckon/ or skills/ still passes.
3. Negative control: removing one alias from the table makes that name's fixture row fail to normalise.

Do not edit reckon/crew/dispatch.py or reckon/cli.py; they are on hold for a module split. If a crew view needs a cli.py change, report it as a follow-on instead. Gate: tests/test_old_names_resolve.py, every tests/ file that imports reckon.ledger, reckon.crew.recovery, reckon.mcp_views or reckon.crew.reports, and the routing-identifier leak test. Build that list from your head tree with grep -l, and keep only test_*.py modules. Run with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta. If the list is over 120 files, split each arm into two foreground halves of under 40 minutes each. Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/lane-and-model-routing/old-names-resolve.html.
